00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.210
that are probably
most impactful for you

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:52.150
as a cloud user or a
potential cloud user,

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:55.330
and that's data centers
and renewable energy.

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:58.570
And within these
two areas, we've

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:01.660
really taken that
sustainability mission to heart

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:05.230
by innovating and
building more technology

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:07.120
back into our
environmental practices

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.000
to effectively make
them more sustainable.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.460
By pushing our
innovation upstream,

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.500
you as a user downstream
get a better experience.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.080
So I'll take a
second to highlight

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.550
some of those areas,
essentially, the stuff that

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:24.100
can only get from Google Cloud.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:28.060
First, data centers are at
the heart of our company

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.630
in everything that we do.

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:32.090
It powers Google
Cloud Platform, it

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:34.810
powers all of the
other Google products

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:37.930
that billions of users
throughout the world use.

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:40.090
And this is really
the critical part

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:43.600
of the sustainability
story for you as a user,

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:46.210
because all of us are
increasingly going digital.

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:50.380
And digital transformation isn't
about just using new technology

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:51.040
stuff.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:54.160
It's honestly about betting your
business on a digital future.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:56.680
And ultimately, you're
going to use more technology

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:00.610
stuff, which means more data
center use and more energy.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:04.250
And with 2% or more of
the world's electricity

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:08.300
already going to data centers,
this is only going to grow.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:10.300
But it's actually one
area where innovation

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.310
can have an incredible impact.

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:14.080
Compared to five
years ago, we actually

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:17.740
deliver seven times the
compute per watt of energy

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:20.380
that we use in our data centers.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:24.730
Google Cloud's actually the
best at getting the most

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.790
out of the energy that we draw.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:28.540
The way that you measure
this is something

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.740
called power usage
effectiveness or PUE.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:35.110
It's calculated by taking
the total energy that you

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:38.500
use in your data center and
dividing that by only the stuff

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.320
that you use to actually
provide computing power.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:45.220
For every watt of energy that
you use, how much are you're

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:47.590
going to have to use
for all the other stuff,

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:50.250
like facilities and cooling and
all the things that make a data

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:51.250
center work?

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:55.810
For us, we only need 11%
extra stuff to do that.

00:04:55.810 --> 00:05:01.000
So it comes down to an average
PUE across our fleet of 1.11.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:06.280
And you as a user of Google
Cloud products and services,

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.870
you get to take
advantage of that.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:11.267
That's 50% better than the
average data center out there.

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:13.100
And that's efficiency
that we deliver to you

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.320
in using our services.

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:20.780
And one of the ways we're able
to achieve that efficiency

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:22.520
is we actually use
our own machine

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:26.000
learning technologies
in our data centers.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.250
When it comes to
controlling a data center,

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:30.800
it's actually a really
complicated and unique beast.

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:32.570
There's millions
of components that

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:36.140
are relatively fickle
to unpredictable changes

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:37.650
in the environment.

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:39.560
So when you're
managing a data center,

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:41.870
trying to manage these
components in a very manual way

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:43.790
is really inefficient.

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:46.910
And kind of out of
the box manufacturing

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:50.190
or control systems,
industrial control systems,

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:52.430
they aren't universally
applicable across the data

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:53.460
center.

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:55.700
So when you're
facing a challenge

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.820
of trying to get better at
predicting unpredictable things

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:01.670
from millions of
inputs, neural networks

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:04.418
can do a really good
job at doing that.

00:06:04.418 --> 00:06:06.710
That's what they're designed
to do-- essentially, learn

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:08.293
from millions of
inputs and get better

00:06:08.293 --> 00:06:09.780
about predicting the future.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:13.200
So our machine learning
actually controls the cooling,

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.950
which is a major part of the
energy draw within a data

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:17.270
center across our fleet.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:23.630
I mentioned the other area being
renewable energy and energy

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:28.190
in general that's critical to
you as a user of Google Cloud.

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:30.740
Running our business
across Google

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:33.920
requires us to use a
lot of electricity.

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:37.970
And combating climate
change requires all of us

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:41.180
to transition to a
clean energy future.

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:44.990
So at Google, we match
every unit of electricity

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:49.070
that we use across our company
with a unit of renewable energy

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:53.450
that we've purchased somewhere
from a zero carbon source.

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:57.150
In pursuing this goal to reach
a 100% match of our energy,

00:06:57.150 --> 00:07:00.890
we became the largest corporate
purchaser of renewable energy

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:02.810
in history.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:05.660
And some of that investment
in renewable energy

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:08.060
actually goes to wind power.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.820
And similar to our
data centers, we

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:15.050
found ways to make unique
use of the Google technology

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:17.440
to help make wind
power more valuable.

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:19.160
So the thing with
renewable energy

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:21.920
is it has to make
financial sense too.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:24.020
That 100% match that
I just showed you,

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:29.120
it represents over $5 billion
in investment from Google.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:35.720
And in order to make financial
sense, the energy that we use,

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:38.930
it has to be more predictable
to be more valuable to the grid.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:40.940
Energy that you can't
predict is actually

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:43.910
less valuable than energy
that you can get consistently

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:45.570
contributing to the grid.

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:50.810
So we apply the ML
to our wind farms

00:07:50.810 --> 00:07:53.000
to predict how they're
going to produce energy

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:55.320
36 hours in advance.

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:57.770
And this machine
learning algorithm

00:07:57.770 --> 00:07:59.870
was essentially trained
on weather forecasts.

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:02.470
And by integrating this
into our wind farms,

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:04.970
we're actually able to increase
the value of the wind energy

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:08.070
that we're producing by 20%.

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:10.520
So with Google working
to make renewable energy

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:14.540
a viable and cost effective
source for our operations,

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:17.750
you as a user get that benefit--

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:20.900
the benefit, essentially,
of being carbon neutral.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:26.180
So any organization that moves
infrastructure or applications

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:31.730
to Google Cloud Platform, you
reduce the net carbon emissions

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:35.210
associated with your usage to 0.

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:39.110
Everything that runs in our
Cloud is net carbon free.

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:41.090
I know I just said the
same thing three times,

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:42.590
but I want to get
this point across.

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:43.940
It's critically important.

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:48.290
If your organization sets
any sort of emissions

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:52.100
or sustainability
goals, this is the part

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:56.060
that enables you, as a developer
or an IT infrastructure person,

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:58.820
to participate in
that goal setting

00:08:58.820 --> 00:09:01.880
and to actually be a
champion for sustainability

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:06.210
and a champion for change
within your organization.

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:10.010
Ultimately, we at Google
invest in sustainability

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:12.290
to empower all of you--

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:15.920
organizations, governments,
nonprofits, individuals--

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:18.620
to use the technology
in our cloud

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.660
and our other
applications to create

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:23.090
a more sustainable world.

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:26.630
One part is the platform,
Google Cloud Platform,

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:28.390
available to you to build on.

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:32.810
We really believe that
in addition to price

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:35.780
and high performance and
reliability of our systems,

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:38.360
you should get sustainability
built into the platform

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:40.250
that you use.

00:09:40.250 --> 00:09:42.170
One of the other
ways we're really

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:47.090
focused on empowering you as
customers is through data.

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:50.450
We all know information that can
help us make better decisions

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:52.070
about our future.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.680
So lots of the other
teams throughout Google,

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:56.930
the Geo team in
particular, works

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:59.540
with research and
environmental organizations

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:02.090
to get the information
that we have

00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:05.330
into the hands of
scientists and policymakers

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:07.170
that can make a difference.

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:09.410
Earth Engine, the
example here, has

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:14.660
enabled 100,000 plus
scientists throughout the globe

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:16.982
to get a deeper
understanding of our planet.

00:10:16.982 --> 00:10:19.190
So there are opportunities
available like this to you

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:20.840
to as a cloud user.

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:23.960
BigQuery in particular has
lots of publicly available

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:27.020
geographic data sets that you
can use and help make better

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:29.480
decisions about our future.

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:33.740
But honestly, the rest is up
to you to take this platform,

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:36.680
to take the data, to take
the partnership that we have

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:38.930
and build for the future.

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:42.110
And I honestly hope you
do, because we've all

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:46.220
seen through the beautiful
very high definition

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:50.180
lens of our next presenter
what's at stake for our planet.

00:10:50.180 --> 00:10:52.760
So without further
ado, I'd like to invite

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:55.220
Melissa Wiley from National
Geographic partners

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:56.040
